Said first party confers upon the trustee the following powers and authority:
(1) Sale of assets. To sell for any purpose any of the assets at any time subject hereto at public or private sale without advertisement at such prices and on such terms and conditions as to it may seem appropriate;
(2) Costs and expenses. To pay and contract to pay out of the income received by the trustee hereunder, all proper costs and expenses incident to the discharge of the duties imposed upon the trustee hereunder, including its own compensation;
(3) Collect income. To collect the income and revenue from all property and assets held hereunder, and the trustee is hereby authorized to give as full receipt and acquittance therefor as said first party could give if this instrument had not been executed;
(4) Foreclosure. To foreclose mortgages on real or personal property, and to sell the same under power, and bid at any sale thereof as trustee, and in the name of said trustee under this agreement, and to take such other steps as in trustee's sole discretion may be necessary and proper to protect and right to rent, operate, manage, improve, control, sell or convey any or all of said assets, pursuant to the terms of this agreement;
(5) Compromise claims. To compromise, settle, and adjust any claim or demand for or against the trust and to agree to any rescission or modification of any contract or agreement affecting the trust;
(6) Vote stock. To vote in person or by proxy any corporate stock or other security and to agree to take any other action in regard to any re-organization, merger, consolidation, bankruptcy, or other procedure, or proceeding, affecting any stock, bond, note or other property;
(7) Court order to exercise powers. To exercise the powers and authority herein given without order of, or report to, any court; and
(8) Reports to court. To be expressly exempt from making any bond, inventory, accounting, appraisal or other reports to any court.
(Ord. No. 77, § (5), 11-4-1968)
